  'Al-alam/alam_0036.jpg': {arabic:'التعليم في ولاية طرابلس',headline:'Education in the State of Tripoli'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0037.jpg': {arabic:'التلفزيون يغزو البلاد العربية - شركة التلفزيون اللبنانية',headline:'Television invades the Arab countries / The Lebanese Television Company'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0038.jpg': {arabic:'التلفزيون اللبناني',headline:'Lebanese Television'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0039.jpg': {arabic:'مغامرات الرواد لاكتشاف القطب الجنوبي / القطب المجمود [مقال]',headline:'"Adventures of the Pioneers in Discovering the South Pole" — historical feature on Antarctic exploration; photos of the expedition ship at port, a bearded explorer, sled team crossing the ice, and penguins gathered around a tracked vehicle; mentions expeditions of Amundsen and Scott (1911), Byrd (1928), and later dates up to 1958'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0040.jpg': {arabic:'البريد المغربي - مشاهد من المغرب / دنلوب DUNLOP - أحسن إطار في مواقع العمل [إعلان]',headline:'"The Moroccan Post" — travel/culture feature with photos of ornate Moorish architecture (mosque minaret and palace facade in Morocco); accompanying poem in classical Arabic / [Full-page ad] Dunlop tires: "The best tire on the worksite" — full range of tires for cars, trucks and heavy machinery; "Dunlop makes the tire that gets the job done best"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0041.jpg': {arabic:'من منتخبات العالم - حسناء شقراء وسمراء تستنشم بشمس يونيه الدافئة',headline:'"World Selections" full-page color portrait — a red-haired starlet reclining on a wicker chair, sunbathing in the warm June sun; caption identifies her as a rising Hollywood/European star whose vocal talent was discovered while she was singing in Yemen, and who now records songs in eight languages [likely Anna Maria Alberghetti or similar]'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0042.jpg': {arabic:'من منتخبات العالم [صورة كاملة الصفحة]',headline:'"World Selections" full-page color pin-up — blonde young woman with a green scarf headband, in a blue polka-dot sundress, leaning on a seaside rock with the sea and shore behind her; a summer beauty shot with no article text'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0043.jpg': {arabic:'ما أغرب هذا العالم! / توأمان يتسابقان للفوز بزوجة / سباق للحصول على قطعة أرض / نفس ما نفيضك حقيقة / طريقة لامتحان نزيه الموظفين / رعب الملح على الجروح',headline:'"How Strange This World Is!" — a novelty/human-interest column with short items: "Twin brothers race to win the same bride" — story from a US town; "A race to win a plot of land" — settlers\' land rush; "Say what you truly feel" — relationship advice piece; "A method for testing employee honesty" — a Portuguese mayor\'s honesty test for staff; "Salt in the wounds" — story of a jewel-theft victim insulted twice by circumstance'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0044.jpg': {arabic:'قصة قصيرة: أحلى من الحب - بقلم وفاء نصر',headline:'Short story: "Sweeter Than Love" — by Wafa Nasr — a romance/psychological piece opening with a woman gazing at old framed photographs; illustrated with a silhouette drawing of a young couple looking into each other\'s eyes'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0045.jpg': {arabic:'للنساء - الاختراع في الأزياء - الأزرق / موديلات مايوهات الصيف',headline:'"For Women" — fashion feature on "Innovation in Fashion — The Color Blue" showcasing the season\'s new blue swimsuits and beach wear; three color model photos: brunette in a white/blue chevron maillot holding an orange beach ball, blonde in a houndstooth co-ord, and a model in a leopard-print one-piece holding snorkel gear'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0046.jpg': {arabic:'الأرض كما يراها العلماء - ومن الانفجارات ما قد يفيد! / الدقيق يتفجر / ما هو الاحتراق؟',headline:'"The Earth as Scientists See It" — new popular-science series — this installment: "...Some Explosions Can Be Useful!" Three sections: (1) "Flour Explodes" — on grain-dust explosions (references the deadly 1944 mill explosion in Kansas that killed 61); (2) "A Violent Bang, and the Car Surges Forward" — how internal-combustion engines work; (3) "What Is Combustion?" — the chemistry of burning; illustrated with cutaway diagrams of a car engine, jet plane, and diesel engine'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0047.jpg': {arabic:'ثياب مطالة للأولاد الذين يقضون إجازتهم على شاطئ البحر / أزياء المصيف [مجموعة موديلات]',headline:'"Long-cut clothes for children spending their vacation at the seaside" — summer resort fashion feature; six color photos of women modeling beachwear (blue-and-white striped rompers, red printed cotton dress, blue-and-white blouse and cropped pants), plus one photo of three children in matching striped tops on a beach'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0048.jpg': {arabic:'الأفلام الجديدة: معركة الجنسين - بطولة كونستانس كامنجز وبيتر سيلرز',headline:'"New Films: The Battle of the Sexes" — film review of the 1960 British comedy starring Constance Cummings and Peter Sellers; four film stills; plot summary: a mild-mannered Scottish accountant clashes with an American businesswoman brought in to modernize his family firm'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0049.jpg': {arabic:'حكايات عن النجوم - الفيس برسلي يعود للشاشة / النقود تجلو صوتها / دروس بيانو كلفت ألف جنيه / مكتشف النجوم يحرص كيف نجم',headline:'"Tales of the Stars" — celebrity gossip column: (1) "Elvis Presley Returns to the Screen" — Elvis back from military service and shooting a new film; photo of Elvis with guitar; (2) "Money Polishes Her Voice" — feature on Doris Day (or similar blonde star), how her recording career funded her voice training; (3) "Piano lessons that cost a thousand pounds" — pianist trained by paid celebrity tutors; (4) "Star-discoverer keeps every star of his" — Hollywood talent-scout profile'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0050.jpg': {arabic:'زواج يتغلب على كل عقبة / سلفيا سيمز للطبيعة المتواضعة / الكشف عنها على طائرة هليكوبتر',headline:'More celebrity news: (1) "A marriage that overcomes every obstacle" — Hollywood actress on her rocky but enduring marriage; boudoir-style photo of her in a fishnet-patterned outfit; (2) "Sylvia Syms — the humble country girl" — profile of British actress Sylvia Syms, praising her modesty; (3) "Discovered aboard a helicopter" — young starlet spotted by a producer during a helicopter ride; portrait with flowers'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0051.jpg': {arabic:'قصة العدد: حقد - بقلم توما خوري / سلطان الظلام (تتمة)',headline:'"Story of the Issue: Rancor" — a short story by Toma Khoury, with cartoon-illustration of a bandaged patient in bed being visited by a doctor / Continuation of an earlier feature titled "The Sultan of Darkness" — literary/moralistic piece'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0052.jpg': {arabic:'طريقة ورندة (تتمة) / يقتل الذباب بالضغط على الزر PIF PAF [إعلان]',headline:'Continuation of a short story titled "Ronda\'s Method" (or "Method and Ronda") — end of the story column / Repeat of the PIF PAF aerosol insecticide full-color ad — "Kills flies at the press of a button, leaves a clean scent in the air. No noise, no mess."'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0053.jpg': {arabic:'الأرض كما يراها العلماء (تتمة) / ٤) ملح البارود والصواريخ / ٥) المواد الشديدة الانفجار / ٦) الفرد نوبل',headline:'"The Earth as Scientists See It" (continuation) — three more sections of the popular-science series on explosions: (4) "Gunpowder and Rockets" — how solid-fuel and liquid-fuel rockets work, with cutaway diagrams of missile stages; (5) "Highly Explosive Materials" — chemistry of nitroglycerin, TNT, dynamite, illustrated with molecular diagrams; (6) "Alfred Nobel" — biographical sketch of the inventor of dynamite and founder of the Nobel Prize'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0054.jpg': {arabic:'أبطالنا القراء [صور رياضيين قراء المجلة]',headline:'"Our Champion Readers" — reader-submitted sports photo montage: a strongman lying under a Volkswagen minibus while the wheels drive over him; a young boxer in the ring; several bodybuilders posing; captions identify readers from Cairo, Beirut, Tripoli (Lebanon) and Damascus with their addresses'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0055.jpg': {arabic:'أبطالنا القراء (تتمة) - أبطال كمال الأجسام والملاكمة',headline:'"Our Champion Readers" (continued) — more bodybuilding and boxing reader photos: Lebanese boxing champion Nassar of Jerusalem; bodybuilders from Damascus, Amman, Cairo and Tripoli in flexing poses, one holding a large trophy; every photo captioned with the reader\'s name and city'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0056.jpg': {arabic:'تتمة توفيق الحكيم / سلطان الظلام (تتمة) / لكل بيت مختار من مراوح جي إي سي G.E.C. [إعلان]',headline:'Continuation of a Tawfiq al-Hakim piece (literary essay/short story) / Continuation of "The Sultan of Darkness" article / [Full-page ad] G.E.C. ceiling and standing fans — "For every house a fan chosen from G.E.C." — illustrated with a cartoon couple in a modern living room under a slow-turning ceiling fan'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0057.jpg': {arabic:'العالم - جميع المعلومات الهامة [ترويسة المجلة] / السطوح التي تبقى جميلة على الدوام - استعمل فورمايكا FORMICA [إعلان]',headline:'Magazine masthead/colophon page: "Al-Alam — for all vital information" — subscription info, distributor list (Egypt, Syria, Iraq, Jordan, Sudan), cover-image caption, and small news items / [Bottom ad] FORMICA laminates for furniture: "Surfaces that stay beautiful forever" — with an illustration of a housewife wiping a Formica-topped table'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0058.jpg': {arabic:'تعليم الكبار واجب على الأهم - بقلم عبد الحسيب أحمد مدير مدرسة أزيلة',headline:'"Adult Education Is the Most Urgent Duty" — feature article by Abd al-Haseeb Ahmad, principal of the Azila school, on the campaign against illiteracy in the Arab world; two photos: a village literacy classroom with an instructor at the blackboard, and men studying in a library reading room'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0059.jpg': {arabic:'أحسن سيكارة في العالم - ستايت اكسبريس ٥٥٥ ثري فايف [إعلان]',headline:'[Full-page color ad] "The best cigarette in the world — State Express 555 (Three Five)" — glamour photograph of a blonde woman lighting her cigarette from the young man beside her, with the yellow-and-red 555 pack on the table and violets in a vase'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0060.jpg': {arabic:'مكافحة الملاريا في السودان [افتتاحية العدد] / فتاة تاهيتي [صورة الغلاف الداخلي]',headline:'Issue\'s main feature title page: "The Fight Against Malaria in Sudan" — with a full-page color portrait of a smiling Tahitian young woman by the sea, and a note: "A Tahitian girl — enjoy her charm in the photographs published in the inside pages"; bottom strip lists issue price by country (Egypt 20m, Sudan 20 piasters, Iraq 20 fils, Jordan 20 fils, Libya 20m, Syria 25 piasters, Lebanon 25 piasters, Morocco 50 francs, Tunisia 50m)'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0061.jpg': {arabic:'مكافحة الملاريا في السودان - نتائج تبشر بنجاح كامل / في الدلتا والنيل الأزرق',headline:'"The Fight Against Malaria in Sudan — Results Point to Complete Success" — long feature on the joint Sudanese-WHO anti-malaria campaign in the Nile Delta and Blue Nile regions; explains DDT spraying, testing, health-worker training; photo of three barefoot Sudanese children (probably from an anti-malaria awareness campaign) sitting in front of a hut'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0062.jpg': {arabic:'جهود اليونسكو ومنظمة الصحة العالمية [تتمة] / كيف يحمل الفريق أفراده / نتائج المكافحة / خطة السودان لعشرين سنة',headline:'Continuation of the Sudan malaria feature — photos of the mobile spray-team pickup truck loaded with equipment, health workers vaccinating a village child, and villagers receiving instructions; sections on how the field team is organized, campaign results by district, and Sudan\'s 20-year malaria-eradication plan'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0063.jpg': {arabic:'البنك العثماني - يقوم بجميع أعمال البنوك [إعلان] / دنلوب DUNLOP - الإطار الجبار للمحمولات الثقيلة [إعلان]',headline:'[Full-page bank ad] The Ottoman Bank — headquartered in Turkey, paid capital 5,000,000 Turkish liras — services all commercial banking needs; lists branches in Sudan (Khartoum, Khartoum North, Cassala, Omdurman, Wad Madani, Wadi Halfa, Port Sudan) and around the world (Turkey, Cyprus, Iraq, Jordan, Doha [Arabian Gulf], Kenya, Uganda, Southern Rhodesia); London and Paris addresses given / [Bottom ad] Dunlop "Powergrip Major" — the mighty tire for heavy trucks — plus a list of Dunlop distributors across the Arab world'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0064.jpg': {arabic:'مغارة جعيتا في لبنان - بقلم إلياس مقدسي إلياس [أعجوبة الدنيا الثامنة في السحر والفن والجمال]',headline:'"The Jeita Grotto in Lebanon" — travel feature by Elias Moqaddasi Elias, subtitled "The Eighth Wonder of the World in enchantment, art and beauty"; opens with a large teal-tinted photograph of visitors being punted on a wooden boat through the illuminated cave, past massive stalactites and stalagmites in Lebanon\'s famous Jeita cave system'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0065.jpg': {arabic:'تطور قانون الطيران / حرية الصعود إلى الجو / سيادة الدولة على الفضاء الجوي / حرية القضاء الأعلى',headline:'"The Evolution of Aviation Law" — historical/legal feature on the development of international aviation law from the Wright Brothers\' 1903 flight through the 1919 Paris Convention and the 1944 Chicago Convention; sections on: (1) freedom of ascent, (2) national sovereignty over airspace, (3) freedom of the upper skies (space law); photos of an early Otto Lilienthal glider and other pioneer flying machines'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0066.jpg': {arabic:'حدائق كيو - أعظم حدائق العالم لدراسة فصائل النبات',headline:'"Kew Gardens — the world\'s greatest gardens for the study of plant species" — feature on London\'s Royal Botanic Gardens (Kew), founded 1759, celebrating its 200th anniversary in 1959; photos of Kew\'s famed Palm House glasshouse with visitors strolling in front, and botanists at work indexing herbarium specimens; explains the gardens\' role in cataloguing plant species from across the British Empire'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0067.jpg': {arabic:'جمال صانع - جلاديس - من الحميدي الهادي',headline:'"Manufactured Beauty — Gladys — from Al-Hamidi Al-Hadi" — photo feature on 19-year-old Tahitian girl Gladys, discovered by the magazine\'s photographer while on holiday at the Pacific beach; two color photos: Gladys posing on a picnic bench at the seaside in a blue bikini, and lying on her stomach on the sand at the water\'s edge'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0068.jpg': {arabic:'من منتخبات العالم [صورة كاملة الصفحة - فتاة تاهيتي]',headline:'"World Selections" full-page portrait — close-up color photo of a young Tahitian woman with long dark hair and a green-and-blue tie-front bikini top, looking out at the sea from a boardwalk; a beauty portrait with no accompanying article text'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0069.jpg': {arabic:'جهود اليونسكو [تتمة عن مكافحة الملاريا] / محطة تجريبية زراعية',headline:'Continuation of the anti-malaria/UNESCO feature — photos of Western researchers examining specimens under a microscope, a farm-hand working the fields with a hoe, and a Sudanese village school building; explanation of the joint UNESCO / WHO agricultural training station work in Sudan'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0070.jpg': {arabic:'للنساء - آخر ما وصلت إليه صيحات الموضة في باريس',headline:'"For Women" — Paris fashion spread showcasing the season\'s newest looks; six color photos of models in tailored suits, plaid checked coats, a knitted hat with a light-brown belted coat, a black-and-white houndstooth blouse-and-skirt with matching black gloves, and a red top with a lipstick-pink knee-length skirt; short captions on cut, fabric, and where to wear each look'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0071.jpg': {arabic:'حكايات عن النجوم - يول برنر يتلقى «رزمة»! / رأى زوجته على كل جدار',headline:'"Tales of the Stars" — celebrity gossip page: (1) "Yul Brynner receives a \'package\'!" — brief item about the actor; large color photo of Ginger Rogers (or a Follies Bergère-style dancer) in a white feather-and-corset costume with a bright orange plume; (2) "He saw his wife on every wall" — story of a jealous husband haunted by his wife\'s photos plastered as advertising on city walls'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0072.jpg': {arabic:'نزاع عنيف على ممثلة / عمل المزرعة أعطاها قواماً جميلاً / ممثلة له فلسفة خاصة / بكرا العناية لنفسه / الآباء يقتفون أثر الآباء / التعويضات أغنت الممثل الغني - جيري لويس / جين سيمز',headline:'"Tales of the Stars" continued: (1) "A fierce dispute over an actress" — Jean Simmons (photo left) at the center of a studio contract battle; (2) "Farm work gave her a beautiful figure" — starlet who trains at a country farm; (3) "An actress with her own philosophy" — brief profile with a starlet in a mannish look; (4) "He looks after himself" — Robert Kennedy-like young man photo; (5) "Sons follow in their fathers\' footsteps" — famous-family Hollywood children; (6) "Compensation enriched the wealthy actor" — Jerry Lewis (photo at bottom right) and a lawsuit payout'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0073.jpg': {arabic:'قصة العدد: حرمان - قصة جديدة بقلم سمير شيخاني / في العدد القادم هدية مجانية للقراء - صورة بالألوان الطبيعية لنجمة السينما المشهورة تارا لين',headline:'"Story of the Issue: Deprivation" — a new short story by Samir Sheikhani; illustrated with a stylized headshot of a woman holding a folded letter in her mouth / [Sidebar promo] "Free Gift in the Next Issue" — natural-color photograph of famous cinema star "Tara Lynn" (or similar) for readers who ensure they get the next issue'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0074.jpg': {arabic:'مختارات من صور القراء / تونس قارب الجحيم [رسم كاريكاتير سياسي]',headline:'"Selections from Readers\' Photographs" — photo montage submitted by readers: view of Rawda garden gazebo in Alexandria; a fisherman\'s stall; a pelican-like bird; villagers by a fortress on the Red Sea; a horseman rearing on a stallion in Jordan; a Nile boat and other landscapes; each with a caption naming the reader-photographer and city / Political cartoon: "Tunisia — Boat of Hell" — with a giant flexed arm holding a knife over a small figure with a small caricature representing the Tunisian Republic during the Bizerte crisis (early 1960s)'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0075.jpg': {arabic:'الأرض كما يراها العلماء - الإلكترونات تستطيع التجول / ١) هل تدري أن الضوء يكهرب؟ / ٢) أنواع مختلفة من الذرات',headline:'"The Earth as Scientists See It" — new installment of the popular-science series: "Electrons Can Travel!" — sections (1) "Do You Know That Light Can Electrify?" — on the photoelectric effect, with photo of a photoelectric solar cell used on a satellite; (2) "Different Kinds of Atoms" — atomic structure explanation with diagrams of nuclei and orbiting electrons; also a diagram of a vacuum tube (electron valve)'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0076.jpg': {arabic:'أبطالنا القراء - مثل لأصحاب الأجسام الكاملة',headline:'"Our Champion Readers — Bodybuilders\' Portraits" — reader photo feature: top image of two boys pulling on a rope for a strength-training exercise in a park; below, individual portraits of six young men flexing biceps and posing bodybuilder-style, each captioned with name, city and country (Egypt, Syria, Jordan)'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0077.jpg': {arabic:'أبطالنا القراء (تتمة) - أعضاء نادى الجمال العربي في رياضة كمال الأجسام',headline:'"Our Champion Readers" (continued) — bodybuilder photo grid: eight more reader portraits from Cairo, Damascus, Alexandria, Suez, plus a top photo of a weight-lifter squatting with a heavy barbell (Adel Nour Al-Din, 185 kg) and a group of four flexing men (Nassif, Anton, Pierre and Boris)'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0078.jpg': {arabic:'بقية «فون ولياس» / لكل بيت مختار من مراوح جي إي سي G.E.C. [إعلان]',headline:'Continuation of a translated article on the German rocket scientist Werner von Braun (referred to as "Von Weliyas") — his 1945 surrender to US forces in the Alps and his work on American rockets / [Full-page repeat ad] G.E.C. ceiling fans — "For every home a fan chosen from G.E.C."'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0079.jpg': {arabic:'ما أغرب هذا العالم! / هل تلبس الحيوانات بسرعة؟ / أسورة صائغة كهرباء القيمة / ثروة كهوف في الرمال / حصان يبكي في سرير',headline:'"How Strange This World Is!" — novelty/trivia column with short items: "Do animals dress fast?" — humorous anecdote about a costumed horse in a bedroom (illustrated with a photo of a horse in pajamas standing by a bed); "A goldsmith\'s bracelet worth a fortune in electricity"; "Cave treasures in the sand"; "A horse crying in bed"; and "عزت تعجب بالورعان الغني"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0080.jpg': {arabic:'نصائح الطبيب - تعقيم الرضوض / أحسن سيكارة في العالم - ستايت اكسبريس ٥٥٥ ثري فايف [إعلان]',headline:'"The Doctor\'s Advice" — medical column: how to disinfect and treat bruises, abrasions and small wounds — proper first-aid procedure, iodine and mercurochrome, when to see a doctor; illustrated with cartoon of doctor consulting patient / [Half-page ad] "The best cigarette in the world — State Express 555 (Three Five)" — with cartoon of a housewife spraying a scared mouse: "— What? Mice?! ...I saw one today, a big one!" — humor strip alongside the yellow-red 555 pack'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0081.jpg': {arabic:'توزيع الأراضي / معجزة الأردن / المسجد الحسيني في عمّان',headline:'"Land Distribution" (top banner) / "The Miracle of Jordan" — main feature on Jordan\'s economic and agricultural development; full-width photo of Amman\'s Al-Husseini Mosque and the surrounding old market with the twin minarets against the hillside city; statistics on Jordan\'s cultivable area, expanding population (about 1.4 million), and land-reform progress'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0082.jpg': {arabic:'مؤتمرات شيراز - مدينة العلم والورد - بقلم الدكتور نقولا زيادة',headline:'"The Conferences of Shiraz — City of Learning and Roses" — travel/culture article by Dr. Nicola Ziadeh (Nicolas Ziadeh); two photos of Persian garden scenes in Shiraz (a shrine kiosk in a walled courtyard, and cypress-lined promenades of the Bagh-e Eram gardens); text on Shiraz\'s cultural heritage, the 800,000-population city, its Islamic monuments, and its literary festivals'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0083.jpg': {arabic:'قطع أوروبية من القرن السابع عشر / مزاول للجيب - طلائع الساعات الحديثة',headline:'"European Timepieces of the Seventeenth Century" — feature on antique timekeeping: an ornate Italian dragon-form standing clock; a rare four-hourglass sand-clock; illustrations of a 17th-century Cavalier and an Elizabethan lady in period dress; below: "Pocket Sundials — Forerunners of the Modern Watch" — showing folding portable sundials and pocket compasses from the 16th–17th centuries'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0084.jpg': {arabic:'إنكلترا في العهد السكسوني / ٣) النار / ٤) الرمل / ٥) الشمعة',headline:'"England in the Saxon Age" — historical/technology feature on how the Saxons kept time: (3) Fire clocks — burning tapers marked with hour-lines; (4) Sandglasses; (5) Candle clocks (King Alfred the Great is credited with the earliest candle clock); illustrations of a Saxon warrior in cape and chainmail with sword and mace, plus early clock artifacts'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0085.jpg': {arabic:'السمنة وإنقاص الوزن - ماذا؟ هل تحفر قبرك بشوكة وسكين؟',headline:'"Obesity and Weight Loss — What? Are you digging your own grave with a fork and knife?" — health feature warning about overeating; illustrated with a striking full-page cartoon of a grinning fat man about to devour a whole roast turkey with a knife and fork; explains that obesity has become a major cause of death, describes the medical risks, and outlines calorie-controlled dieting principles'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0086.jpg': {arabic:'من منتخبات العالم [صورة كاملة الصفحة - حسناء بقميص خضر]',headline:'"World Selections" full-page color portrait — brunette starlet in an emerald green scallop-cut strapless bodice, sitting against an orange-and-white striped beach cabana; a summer beauty shot with no article text'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0087.jpg': {arabic:'الراحة التامة - دنلوبيللو Dunlopillo - المطاط الإسفنجي [إعلان] / السطوح التي تبقى لامعة ونظيفة دائماً - فورمايكا FORMICA [إعلان]',headline:'[Top ad] Dunlopillo latex-foam mattresses and pillows: "Perfect Comfort — Dunlopillo, the foam-rubber mattress" — with cartoon of a smiling woman in bed; "no other mattress in the world is better" / [Bottom ad] Formica laminates for furniture: "Surfaces that stay shiny and clean forever" — cartoon of a shopkeeper behind a clean Formica counter'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0088.jpg': {arabic:'المرأة في السودان [مقال] / خالة زاهرة في الكلية الطبية بالخرطوم',headline:'"Women in Sudan" — feature on the changing role of women in Sudanese public life; photos of "Aunt Zahira," a Sudanese medical student, examining a hospitalized patient at Khartoum\'s medical college — she is one of the first Sudanese women to enter the medical profession; also a photo of an activist speaking at a women\'s federation microphone; text describes struggles for women\'s political and educational rights'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0089.jpg': {arabic:'المرأة في السودان (تتمة) / خلع بيري ونقاش أحد مراكز رعاية الطفولة والأمومة بمدينة المرغى',headline:'"Women in Sudan" (continued) — more photos of Sudanese women\'s public activities: a fashionable woman photographed at home; a mother-and-child health clinic in the town of Al-Marghay showing a nurse weighing a Sudanese toddler on a balance; a group of professional women mingling at a reception; and a woman scientist working at a laboratory microscope'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0090.jpg': {arabic:'للنساء - الفتى الملون [مجموعة موديلات]',headline:'"For Women" — fashion feature showcasing the season\'s youthful summer looks; main photo of a young model in a red-and-white gingham fit-and-flare dress and white flat shoes standing by a stone wall; two inset photos of a floral-print sleeveless dress and a copper-woven high-heel shoe; captions describe fabrics, cuts and price categories'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0091.jpg': {arabic:'للنساء - الجرزاية المفردة التخطيط [موضة كنزات مقلمة]',headline:'"For Women" — knitwear fashion feature titled "The Single-Striped Sweater"; four photos of models in the season\'s striped-knit tops: brunette in a vertical black-and-white ringer top with headband, blonde in a boat-neck top with a scarf and pale trousers, and close-ups of a bangle and hooped-stripe sleeve details; text describes wool blends and how to wear the look'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0092.jpg': {arabic:'عن النجوم - زوجة تدفع الثمن / أكبر استديوهات العالم في أحضان الأرض / ممثلة الكليبرة تود اللهو في فلم عربي / الممرضة الجميلة',headline:'"About the Stars" — celebrity news page: (1) "A wife pays the price" — Hollywood story of a starlet whose jealous rages cost her a role; three photos of the actress: at a hair salon, in a headshot, and in an ornate print blouse; (2) "The world\'s largest studios in the bosom of the earth" — feature on underground film sets; (3) "The Clay-berry actress wants to appear in an Arab film" — starlet who wants an Arabic-language role; (4) "The Beautiful Nurse" — glamour shot of a model in a bathing suit'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0093.jpg': {arabic:'حكايات - اختطفها لِيلقيها الغناء / جاء من الشعر المستعار / ترويض ممثلة شرسة',headline:'"Tales" — celebrity gossip page: (1) "She was kidnapped so she\'d sing!" — story about a starlet abducted to force her to perform (Italian actress); full-length photo of her seated on the floor in a slinky black cocktail dress; (2) "He came out of the wigs" — item about a Hollywood star who owes his career to elaborate hairpieces; (3) "Taming a fierce actress" — profile of a difficult star tamed by a strict director; small inset headshot of a smiling starlet'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0094.jpg': {arabic:'بينما كنت في طريقي إلى غرفة الملابس (تتمة قصة) / قصة كأنشتاين أعرب لنا رسبت / رسم ملاكمة',headline:'Continuation of a short story ("While I was on my way to the dressing room…"): boxing-themed romance/drama; large full-color illustration of two boxers grappling in a boxing ring, painted in punchy red-and-white; text continues from an earlier page (referenced page 39)'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0095.jpg': {arabic:'قصة العدد: عمران - بقلم سمير عبد العزيز صنى / لجميع الأجهزة والأدوات الكهربائية G.E.C. [إعلان]',headline:'"Story of the Issue: Omran" — a new short story by Samir Abd al-Aziz Sanad, opening on a scene at a lakeside near a village / [Bottom half-page ad] G.E.C. (General Electric Company Ltd. of England): "For all electrical equipment and appliances" — illustration of a G.E.C. power-plant facility with turbines and generators; list of G.E.C. agents across Iraq, Jordan, Egypt, Syria, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Kuwait and Sudan'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0096.jpg': {arabic:'الأرض كما يراها العلماء - إن في «الشرر» بياناً وسحراً! / ١) هل تدري أن البرق يقدح في الثانية الواحدة ١٠٠ قدحة؟ / ٢) الشرارة «كهرباء» تخترق الهواء / ٣) عداد «جايجر»',headline:'"The Earth as Scientists See It" — installment: "There is Explanation and Enchantment in the \'Spark\'!" — three sections: (1) "Did you know lightning strikes 100 times per second?" — atmospheric electricity and the physics of lightning, illustrated with a boy at a window watching a bolt strike over a city; (2) "The Spark (\'Electricity\') Pierces the Air" — dielectric breakdown of gases; (3) "The Geiger Counter" — how ionization detectors measure radiation, with a diagram of a Geiger tube'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0097.jpg': {arabic:'نصائح الطبيب - أمراض الطفل / حيث صعوبات الطريق شديدة هذا الإطار الأشد - دنلوب باور كريب ميجر [إعلان]',headline:'"The Doctor\'s Advice" — pediatric health column: how to recognize and treat childhood diseases (measles, whooping cough, mumps, digestive complaints), when to seek professional help; small illustration of the medical-advice masthead / [Bottom ad] Dunlop "Powergrip Major" tire: "Where the road is toughest, this is the toughest tire" — designed to withstand the harshest conditions, for heavy trucks and off-road vehicles'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0098.jpg': {arabic:'حكام الإمارات المتصالحة في ساحل عمان [مقال]',headline:'"The Rulers of the Trucial States on the Oman Coast" — feature on the Trucial sheikhs (the emirates that would become the UAE in 1971); grid of seven portraits of ruling sheikhs — Sheikh Shakhbut of Abu Dhabi, Sheikh Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum of Dubai, the ruler of Sharjah, of Ajman, of Fujairah, of Umm Al Quwain, of Ras Al Khaimah — plus a photo of a modern white 3-storey Ottoman Bank building in one of the towns with 1950s American cars parked in front; small map of the Trucial Coast'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0099.jpg': {arabic:'العش... أكثر أعداء الإنسان ضرراً!',headline:'"The Moth… Man\'s Most Damaging Enemy!" — pest-control feature on the clothes moth (illustrated with an enormous yellow-and-black photographic close-up of a moth on a black ground); explains the moth\'s life cycle, its enormous economic damage to wool, fur and stored fabrics; recommendations on prevention, mothballs, chemical treatments, and modern mothproofing'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0100.jpg': {arabic:'العش (تتمة) / تجارب العلماء / ٤ أجيال قادرة على تلف أكثر من ١٨ بدلة صوفية أو أكثر من ٤٦ فستاناً صوفياً',headline:'"The Moth" (continued) — scientific research on moth breeding; photos of scientists holding specimen jars, a scientist examining insects under lab conditions, greenhouse experiments, and a fashion illustration of a couple in a chic red-and-black plaid dress with a matching man\'s suit; caption warns: "A single moth\'s four generations can ruin more than 18 wool suits or 46 wool dresses"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0101.jpg': {arabic:'للنساء - موديلات فساتين وأزياء متنوعة [٦ صور]',headline:'"For Women" — Paris/Milan fashion grid: six model photos numbered 3–8: (3) tan skirt-suit with a Cocker Spaniel on a leash; (4) full-skirt printed dress with white gloves; (5) sky-blue chiffon dress with pleated skirt; (6) chestnut-brown paisley knit dress; (7) white belted trench-jacket over a slim skirt; (8) leopard-print full-skirt dress with belted waist and matching hood'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0102.jpg': {arabic:'تعاون عالمي على محاربة السل / الفلبين / بقنوة',headline:'"Global Cooperation to Fight Tuberculosis" — feature on WHO/UNICEF\'s global anti-TB program; large photo of two surgeons in an operating theater; text: "The Philippines received from Filipino compensation funds all the medical and hospital equipment necessary to protect the health of mothers and children in a large area of the Philippine Islands" — plus figures on TB deaths and BCG-vaccination goals'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0103.jpg': {arabic:'الجمهورية العربية المتحدة - دمشق / طلائع جديدة تقاوم بالغم / ليبيا',headline:'"The United Arab Republic — Damascus" — TB campaign photo essay: a WHO mobile field clinic bus parked outside a Damascus school; women waiting in the clinic corridor; nurses testing children for TB with a skin test; text on how the campaign is deploying BCG vaccine in Syria and Egypt / Sidebar: "Libya — a follow-up class trained on the BCG vaccine in Tripoli, home of Libya\'s TB fighters"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0104.jpg': {arabic:'فيتنام / هونغ كونغ / الأفغان / اكوادور [صور من الحملة العالمية لمحاربة السل]',headline:'"Vietnam / Hong Kong / Afghanistan / Ecuador" — global TB campaign photo grid: (top) a Vietnamese doctor examines a child (fear-of-injections photo); nurse gives a Hong Kong child a BCG vaccination in a school clinic; (bottom) a doctor conducts a chest exam of a bare-chested elderly man in an Afghan clinic in Kabul; a lab worker prepares TB vaccines in a Latin American clinic'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0105.jpg': {arabic:'كهن يعد لنفسه مقبراً / عرس لا يعيب ضياع الوقت / إعلان أنبوب مام MUM الجديد [إعلان]',headline:'"Strange but True" novelty column: photo of a fantastical pile of bulbous natural rock formations resembling a giant beehive — geological curiosity from Tayvan / "A priest who prepares his own grave" — brief; "A wedding that doesn\'t waste time" — human-interest story / [Bottom half-page ad] MUM anti-perspirant (Rollette and paste) from Bristol-Myers, London and New York: "The new MUM tube — reveals your natural charm" — with cartoon of a woman applying deodorant, and package shots of the MUM Rollette and MUM cream'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0106.jpg': {arabic:'المرأة العربية سلطانة بيتها',headline:'"The Arab Woman — Queen of Her Home" — feature on the modern Arab housewife\'s role in running the household economy; two photos of a stylish modern living room with wood-lattice screens, area rug and low-slung sofa; and reception salon with a Louis-style side chair and vases; text argues that the housewife controls a significant share of family income and civic life'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0107.jpg': {arabic:'من منتخبات العالم [صورة كاملة الصفحة - فتاة إيطالية في مايو]',headline:'"World Selections" full-page color portrait — young Italian starlet Colada (or similar) kneeling in the surf at the water\'s edge in a peach-colored one-piece swimsuit; short caption identifies her as an Italian actress recently discovered on the shores of Positano, chosen for a starring film role'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0108.jpg': {arabic:'الأرض كما يراها العلماء - النخل - سيدة الغلال (تتمة) / الفصيلة البلاذمية / أسبرو ASPRO [إعلان] / شامبو درين DRENE [إعلان]',headline:'"The Earth as Scientists See It" — feature: "The Palm Tree — Queen of Crops" (continuation) with sections on Batatas (potatoes), root vegetables, wheat and rice cultivation, and various vegetable species; photos of potato crops in seed trays; text explains how a single seed potato can yield 90–120 kilograms per hectare / [Bottom-left ad] ASPRO tablets: "Aspro gives you the strength to overcome pain" / [Bottom-right ad] DRENE shampoo: "Nourishes hair and gives it luster"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0109.jpg': {arabic:'للنساء - للأمهات [مجموعة أزياء وموضة سيدات]',headline:'"For Women — For Mothers" — spring fashion feature; two model photos: a brunette in a boxy pale-blue skirt-suit and long white gloves, and a redhead in a golden-yellow bouclé skirt-suit with matching pillbox hat; the "For Mothers" sidebar discusses fabric choices, styling for the modern mom, and answers to readers\' letters on children\'s health'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0110.jpg': {arabic:'روبرت أصغر الكابلة / الفلم الأميركي - هبت الريح مع الحب [شريط أفلام]',headline:'"Bob Hope, the Youngest of the Kids" — celebrity/family feature: three film-still photos of an American drama: (top) actor arguing on a Victorian porch and a starlet in a rowboat; (middle) a couple in a bedroom scene with a redheaded woman screaming beside a Big Ben alarm clock; (bottom) a Cary Grant-like leading man in a family portrait with three children and his wife — a family drama film review'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0111.jpg': {arabic:'جين منسفيلد توقف مناورة عسكرية / أجرة تعرف التعليم البيتني / موقف سينمائي رائع / السعادة غير المال والشهرة والجمال / من عكسه غض الطرف عنها',headline:'"About the Stars" gossip page: (1) "Jayne Mansfield halts a military maneuver" — brief on the actress causing an on-set disruption; blonde-hair Jayne photo top left; (2) "An actress who is a homemaker" — starlet perched on a wrought-iron chair with a pet dog; (3) "A wonderful cinema moment" — brief item on a memorable film scene; (4) "Happiness is not money, fame or beauty" — inset article; (5) portrait of a brunette starlet in a bath towel, "Whose beauty could no one look away from?"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0112.jpg': {arabic:'قصة العدد: صديقة الأطفال - حيلة البغاء في إخفاء الجثة المسمومة أنقذت صاحبها من عذاب الضمير والنار وتركت القدر يصدر حكمه...',headline:'"Story of the Issue: The Children\'s Friend" — a crime/psychological short story: "The parrot\'s trick in hiding the poisoned corpse saved its owner from the torment of conscience and hell, and left fate to render its verdict…"; large dramatic illustration of a startled parrot bursting into a room where a man reacts in horror as another man watches — the parrot appears to reveal a hidden crime'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0113.jpg': {arabic:'حكايات عن النجوم - أروع الراقصات ولدت كسيحة / زوجان يتفرقان على أنواع الغزل / حبا الممثل الكبير شعلا / عدة حقيقي عمل أدوار العمدة',headline:'"Tales of the Stars" — celebrity news: (1) "The most amazing dancer was born crippled" — inspiring story of a paralyzed girl who became a professional dancer; large color photo of a redhead in a burgundy leotard-and-hose performing a raised-leg pose; (2) "A couple splits over threads of yarn" — celebrity divorce over knitting; small inset of a young couple with a puppy; (3) "Love kindled the great actor" — Frank Sinatra-like crooner headshot; (4) "A real feud plays the roles of the mayor" — brief on a stage actor'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0114.jpg': {arabic:'قصة العدد: عشقت ابنة سفاح... - كل واحد من سكان القرية كان يرجف رعباً من أبيها وأنا أعشقهم ولكن... لو كانت ابنة الشيطان لما ترددت في زواجها',headline:'"Story of the Issue: I Loved a Murderer\'s Daughter…" — a romantic thriller short story: "Every villager trembled in fear of her father, yet I loved them. But even if she had been the devil\'s daughter, I would not have hesitated to marry her"; illustrated with a striking portrait of a wide-eyed brunette leaning on a mantelpiece, and a sepia-toned inset of two women in period dress in a doorway'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0115.jpg': {arabic:'في هوليوود حيث تتلاشى أعمار النجوم',headline:'In Hollywood where stars\' ages fade away.'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0116.jpg': {arabic:'أشكر كولجيت فهو سبب نجاحي - كولجيت COLGATE بمعجون أسنان GARDOL [إعلان]',headline:'[Full-page ad] Colgate Dental Cream with Gardol: "I thank Colgate — it\'s the reason for my success" — testimonial-style advertisement showing an airline stewardess and cartoon scenes of her at work (welcoming passengers, checking in a business traveler, receiving a bouquet by the Leaning Tower of Pisa); slogan: "Colgate freshens the mouth, cleans and protects teeth" — pack shot of the classic red-and-white Colgate tube'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0117.jpg': {arabic:'هذه هي المساعدات القيمة... / تعليم الأمهات في الإقليم الجنوبي من الجمهورية العربية المتحدة طريقة إطعام أولادها الصغار حبوب الفيتامين المختلفة / جهود صندوق إغاثة الأطفال الدولي في البلاد العربية',headline:'"These Are the Valuable Aid Contributions…" — feature title spread for a report on UNICEF\'s work in the Arab world; large color photo of a young Sudanese/Egyptian mother holding her infant while a health worker holds a UNICEF box of Vitamin A+D beads and demonstrates administering vitamin supplements to a baby; text on the U.N. children\'s fund\'s programs in Egypt, Sudan and other Arab countries'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0118.jpg': {arabic:'أنواع المساعدة للاجئين الفلسطيني / الجمهورية العربية المتحدة',headline:'"Types of Aid to Palestinian Refugees" — sidebar on UNICEF/UNRWA emergency assistance to Palestinian refugee camps in Jordan and Syria, with photo of a physician in dark goggles (X-ray goggles) examining a baby for skin/eye disease at a Cairo mobile clinic; "The United Arab Republic" — a UNICEF mobile clinic in an Egyptian village, with health workers vaccinating villagers and distributing food supplements'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0119.jpg': {arabic:'مكافحة الملاريا وغيرها في العراق / في السودان وعدن والصومال ولبنان / مساعدات لبلاد الشرق الأدنى',headline:'"Fighting Malaria and Other Diseases in Iraq" — photos of a Bristol-Myers vitamin-drink pharmacy dispensing bottles to a mother, and a doctor with a WHO campaign banner examining a child in Beirut; text describes UNICEF aid to Iraq, Sudan, Aden, Somalia and Lebanon for anti-malaria, TB, and eye-disease campaigns'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0120.jpg': {arabic:'أحدث دور السينما المفتوحة في بومباي / لجميع الأجهزة والأدوات الكهربائية G.E.C. [إعلان] / مشاهد من فيلم روبن هود',headline:'"The Newest Cinema Complex Open in Bombay" — photo feature on the Maratha Mandir cinema in Bombay with poster for a Hindi film; film-review stills from a Hollywood family drama — a housewife in a domestic scene, a leading man on a bed with a wounded soldier, and a couple in a rock grotto with candles / [Left half-page ad] G.E.C. English electrical equipment for all industrial and commercial applications'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0121.jpg': {arabic:'الاكتشاف صنع المرضى - السرطان أسبابه وأعراضه',headline:'"The Diseases That Discovery Creates — Cancer: Its Causes and Symptoms" — long health feature: photo of a scientist operating a centrifuge/cyclotron in a research lab; photo of a heavy traffic jam representing urban pollution; extreme close-up photo of an ashtray with a lit cigarette next to reading glasses (symbolizing tobacco\'s role in cancer); sections on cancers of the mouth, lung, skin, blood, breast; explains carcinogens and early-warning signs'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0122.jpg': {arabic:'حكايات عن النجوم - نجمة تؤمن بالتنجيم / سعادة في الحب على الشاشة / باتريشيا أوين',headline:'"Tales of the Stars": (1) "A star who believes in astrology" — feature; large color photo of a giggling blonde starlet in denim shorts holding a long fishing rod, standing barefoot; (2) "Happiness in love on the screen" — profile of actress Patricia Owens; portrait of Patricia Owens in a headscarf; (3) "How to sweeten the flavor of a marriage" — brief item'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0123.jpg': {arabic:'نجمة تستمع إلى إرشادات زوجها / أودري هيبورن وزوجها ميل فرير / مهدها كان صندوق خشب / المال غير مهم في نظره',headline:'"Tales of the Stars" (continued): (1) "A star who listens to her husband\'s guidance" — Audrey Hepburn feature; photo of Audrey Hepburn and husband Mel Ferrer; (2) "Her cradle was a wooden crate" — rags-to-riches profile of an Italian starlet (probably Gina Lollobrigida), shown seated barefoot on a haystack in an off-shoulder peasant blouse and orange skirt; (3) "Money is unimportant to him" — Anthony Quinn-like portrait'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0124.jpg': {arabic:'أحب الزواج وأكره الطلاق - جينجر روجرز / المنجمة قالت لها ستتزوجين قريباً - لورين باكال / عشرون عاماً في عيد متواصل - روبرت تايلور',headline:'"Tales of the Stars" continued: (1) "I love marriage and hate divorce" — Ginger Rogers profile; photo of Ginger Rogers dancing in a white gown with two partners; (2) "The astrologer told her: you will marry soon" — Lauren Bacall profile; portrait photo; (3) "Twenty years in a continuous celebration" — Robert Taylor feature; portrait of the actor'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0125.jpg': {arabic:'قصة العدد: الرجل الهائل - أقرب الرحلات في الشاطئ... وسط الظلمات الرقصة عرف عندي كوري نار الحب / كرافن أ CRAVEN A [إعلان]',headline:'"Story of the Issue: The Wandering Man" — a romantic short story; dramatic sailor-hat portrait illustration of a young Navy officer with a small woman\'s face over his shoulder; teaser: "On the closest shore trips, amid the darkness and dance-fires, I recognized my Korean girl by the fire of love" / [Bottom-left ad] Craven A virgin cigarettes: portrait of an elegant woman with a red-white Craven A cigarette pack'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0126.jpg': {arabic:'لكل ساقطة لاقطة يستطيع الفأر الاختباء من الفخ [صور متحركة لفأر يهرب من مصيدة]',headline:'"For Every Trap There\'s an Escape — the Mouse Can Hide from the Snare" — humor/photo-essay: sequence of black-background photographs of a white lab-mouse cleverly maneuvering around a snap trap, stealing the cheese bait, and escaping; captions in cartoon-strip style; below, a data table comparing populations, mice caught and mouse deaths in Britain, USA, France, USSR and Sweden'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0127.jpg': {arabic:'الأرض كما يراها العلماء - الإنسان مجبول من ذرات! / ١) أنت ذرى! / ٢) الذرات صغيرة الحجم جداً / ٣) الذرات قاسية صلبة / ٤) الذرات يمكن تصويرها فوتوغرافياً',headline:'"The Earth as Scientists See It" — new installment: "Man is Made of Atoms!" — four sections: (1) "You Are Atoms!" — atomic-scale intro; (2) "Atoms Are Extremely Small" — with a magnifying-glass illustration; (3) "Atoms Are Hard and Solid" — with ricochet diagram; (4) "Atoms Can Be Photographed" — with electron-microscope image of a crystal lattice caption "A city at night? No — it\'s the first photograph of the atomic structure!"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0128.jpg': {arabic:'٥) حقيقة الذرات لم تكن مجرد مباغتة / ٦) أول من اكتشف الذرة / ٧) فصائل الذرة وأشكالها / ٨) طريقة وزن الذرة / ٩) بعض الذرات قابل للتغير... وبعضها خطر! / ١٠) ما هو جوهر الذرة',headline:'"The Earth as Scientists See It" (continued): (5) "The reality of atoms is no coincidence" — with cameo portraits of John Dalton and Antoine Lavoisier; (6) "Who first discovered the atom?" — Democritus (Ancient Greece) and modern chemists; (7) "Species and shapes of atoms" — diagrams: sodium + chlorine = salt (NaCl); (8) "How atoms are weighed" — mass spectrometry; (9) "Some atoms can change, and some are dangerous!" — isotopes and radioactivity; (10) "What is the essence of the atom?" — teaser for next issue'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0129.jpg': {arabic:'أصحاب الأجسام الكاملة [صور قراء - أبطال كمال أجسام]',headline:'"Bodybuilders" — reader-submitted bodybuilding photo grid: seven black-and-white portraits of young men flexing in the classic bodybuilding stances, including a photo of the winner of the Egyptian/UAR bodybuilding championship at the Armed Forces Cup competition; captions identify each with name, city and country (Egypt, Sudan, Morocco); at bottom a group photo of an entire bodybuilding-club team lined up'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0130.jpg': {arabic:'العدد السادس - السنة الثانية / نوفمبر ١٩٥٨ - ربيع الثاني ١٣٧٨ / جامعة القاهرة / مواطنة ومستشرقوها / بلاد جنوب الجزيرة / صورة بالألوان الطبيعية للنجمة السينمائية باتي رود',headline:'Cover/masthead of Al-Alam magazine — Issue No. 6, Year 2 — November 1958 / Rabi\' al-Thani 1378; large color cover photo of a smiling blonde actress in a floral blue dress in front of an aquarelle vignette of Cairo University\'s clock tower and dome; issue highlights listed on the yellow banner: "Cairo University," "Yugoslavia and its Orientalists," "South-Arabian Countries"; bottom banner: "Free full-color pin-up of cinema star Patti Rowe inside" and issue prices by country (Egypt 20m, Sudan 20 pt, Iraq 20 fils, Jordan 20 fils, Libya 20m, Syria 25 pt, Lebanon 25 pt, Morocco 50 francs, Tunisia 50m)'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0131.jpg': {arabic:'إن سطح المائدة هو الأهم! - فورمايكا FORMICA على جميع الأثاثات [إعلان] / أسبرو ASPRO للتغلب على الألم [إعلان]',headline:'[Top ad] Formica laminates: "The table surface is what matters most!" — for furniture across Syria, Lebanon, Iraq, Jordan, Sudan, Egypt, Saudi Arabia — cartoon of a happy couple sharing coffee at a Formica-topped table with waiter / [Bottom ad] ASPRO tablets to overcome pain — cartoon of a strong man breaking through pain with pills packet; distributor addresses in Iraq, Lebanon, Jordan, Bahrain, Kuwait, Iran, Syria, Egypt, Sudan'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0132.jpg': {arabic:'جامعة القاهرة في خدمة العلم خمسين سنة - بقلم الدكتور جمال الدين الرمادي',headline:'"Cairo University: Fifty Years in the Service of Knowledge" — feature by Dr. Jamal Al-Din Al-Ramadi, marking the university\'s 50th anniversary; full-page hand-painted illustration of the Cairo University main campus — the iconic Great Dome and clock tower framed by palm-lined gardens, ornamental fountains and a period sedan approaching the gates; text on the university\'s founding in 1908, its role in modernizing Egyptian higher education, its faculties, and its regional influence'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0133.jpg': {arabic:'جامعة القاهرة (تتمة) - سفر الجامعة القاهرة ومكسبها بالنكات والمكتبة العامة والعلوم / الطبقات الشرقية في الجامعة / كلية دار العلوم',headline:'"Cairo University" (continued) — architectural sketch pages: an illustration of the university\'s clock-tower plaza and administrative buildings with a period car and pedestrians; illustration of the classical-Islamic Dar Al-Ulum college building (founded 1872) with its wooden mashrabiyya balconies; sections on the university\'s science and humanities faculties, its general library, the Sharif-endowed Eastern classes, and its role as a magnet for students from across the Arab world'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0134.jpg': {arabic:'حكايات عن النجوم - مارلين مونرو تؤمر بإنقاص وزنها / وصايا نفيسة للشباب اليافع / شقيقة بريجيت باردو تخدع هوليود',headline:'"Tales of the Stars": (1) "Marilyn Monroe ordered to lose weight!" — long feature with iconic photo of Marilyn Monroe rehearsing a dance step in a black leotard with a choreographer; small inset of Marilyn playing with a toddler; (2) "Precious advice for young starlets" — grooming and career tips; portrait of a brunette in a black one-piece; (3) "Brigitte Bardot\'s sister fools Hollywood" — story of a look-alike younger sister passing as BB'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0135.jpg': {arabic:'هجرة المولتومين لأميركا / بروكلاكس BROOKLAX الشوكولاتة المسهلة اللذيذة الطعم [إعلان] / كرافن أ CRAVEN A [إعلان]',headline:'Article continuation: "The Mormons\' Migration to America" — with a photo of a busy dockyard filled with 19th-century steamers and sailing ships preparing to carry immigrants across the Atlantic; describes the Mormon Trek and Great Basin settlement / [Bottom-left ad] BROOKLAX chocolate laxative: "We all take Brooklax — the tasty laxative chocolate" — teenagers-and-mother trio smiling / [Bottom-right ad] Craven A Virginia cigarettes with elegant woman portrait'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0136.jpg': {arabic:'الملكة اليصابات الأولى في مملكة الإنكلترا / أوروبا في القرن السادس عشر',headline:'"Queen Elizabeth I of England" — historical feature: full-length portrait of Queen Elizabeth I of England in her royal robes with orb and scepter; a smaller drawing of a Greek/Roman female figure in classical drapery; text discusses the Queen\'s reign, 16th-century Europe, and the rise of European empires; a small inset shows a decorative capital "A" ornament'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0137.jpg': {arabic:'نصائح للأمهات - كيف تختار الفستان لابنتك / أزياء نسائية جديدة',headline:'"Advice for Mothers" — parenting column: how to choose a dress for your young daughter, with photo of a mother helping her little girl into a red dress; large fashion spread of three model photos: a curvy brunette in a black-and-white houndstooth belted dress with black gloves, a blonde in a wine-colored empire-waist chemise, and a redhead in a black long-sleeve bodice with pleated black skirt'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0138.jpg': {arabic:'للنساء - أزياء المصيف [مجموعة أزياء نسائية]',headline:'"For Women" — resort fashion feature: three color model photos: brunette in a coral pink sleeveless coat holding a matching umbrella; blonde in a white sleeveless dress; and a redhead in a vertical navy-and-white pinstripe fitted coat-dress walking down a city street; text describes the season\'s key summer/resort silhouettes and how to accessorize'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0139.jpg': {arabic:'سفينة مهجورة حيرت الدنيا - السفينة «ماري سليست» منشورة الأشرعة متجهة إلى الغرب في المحيط الأطلسي دون أن يكون فيها إنسان - لغز لا يزال يحير الدنيا',headline:'"An Abandoned Ship That Baffled the World" — historical mystery feature on the ghost ship Mary Celeste; large photo of a 19th-century barque under full sail; portraits of Captain Benjamin Briggs and First Officer Albert Richardson; text recounts how the American brig Mary Celeste was found abandoned in mid-Atlantic in December 1872 with sails set, cargo intact and the crew missing without trace — one of the sea\'s enduring mysteries'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0140.jpg': {arabic:'سفينة ماري سليست (تتمة) - في مفرق السفن / أحسن سيكارة في العالم - ستايت اكسبريس ٥٥٥ ثري فايف [إعلان] / شامبو درين DRENE [إعلان]',headline:'"The Mary Celeste" (continued) — closing pages of the ghost-ship story; cartoon illustrations of Captain Briggs at his cabin desk writing in the log, and of the sailors\' quarters below decks; discussion of the various theories: mutiny, piracy, seaquake, methanol fumes / [Bottom-left ad] State Express 555 (Three Five) cigarettes — "The best cigarette in the world" / [Bottom-right ad] Drene shampoo — with woman brushing her hair'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0141.jpg': {arabic:'[صورة كاملة الصفحة - مومياء متجمدة من ضحايا كارثة القطبين]',headline:'Full-page haunting photograph — a frozen, mummified corpse of a polar explorer seated upright in the snow with his frost-covered clothing, wreckage of an aircraft or camp visible in the background; caption: "Is he a prehistoric beast? On the contrary — one of the men of the Polar Air Force, who kept his uniform composure and the strength of a lucky officer, until fate caught his aircraft in the polar wastes"'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0142.jpg': {arabic:'صور غريبة اخترناها لمجموعات القراء / قطة تحاول الإمساك بحبال المكرونة / سيارة معلقة على جدار بيت / طائرة تسقط بين جبلين ثلجيين',headline:'"Strange Photos Selected from the Readers\' Albums" — human-interest photo montage: a strip of five photos of a black-and-white kitten trying to catch strands of spaghetti in cute poses; a photo of a light plane crash-landed diving between two snowy mountain walls onto a car below; a startling news photo of a double-decker bus that has ended up wedged on top of a house wall after an accident'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0143.jpg': {arabic:'من منتخبات العالم [صورة كاملة الصفحة - حسناء بقميص نوم أسود]',headline:'"World Selections" full-page color pin-up — smiling brunette starlet kneeling on an upholstered ottoman, wearing a short black lace-trimmed negligee with a white silk bow; a glamour beauty shot with no accompanying article text'},
  'Al-alam/alam_0144.jpg': {arabic:'من منتخبات العالم [صورة كاملة الصفحة - حسناء بعمامة أرجوانية]',headline:'"World Selections" full-page color close-up portrait — chestnut-haired starlet in profile wearing a purple silk turban, a pearl teardrop earring, red lipstick and a soft pink chiffon top; short caption identifies her as a Mercy Palmer look-alike, one of Hollywood\'s rising elegant new-faces recently featured in a Cairo-produced Arabic film'},
